Candidate Exclusion Criteria
Pattern	Reason
No meaningful US geography	Lacks local targeting relevance
Foreign geographic targeting	Outside the intended market
Dead or unsuitable verticals	No meaningful local call-generation opportunity
Brandable or abstract names	Weak service and buyer intent
Content and media terminology	Indicates readership rather than direct service demand
Hyphens and numeric patterns	Can reduce trust and naming quality
Generic enterprise terminology	Weak consumer-facing call intent
State-only generic combinations	Insufficient local specificity


Scoring Priority Order
When evaluating scoring changes, preserve this priority:
1. Geographic relevance: Identify city and regional signals. Local relevance is foundational.
2. Service relevance: Determine whether the domain represents a callable local service.
3. Name quality: Evaluate readability, spelling, length, and pronounceability.
4. Commercial synergy: Reward combinations where geography, service category, buyer intent, and linguistic relevance reinforce one another.
