Common Mistakes to Avoid
Don't let the Brandable pool near M2. Brandable scoring rewards a different type of asset. Those candidates should not enter local lead-generation evaluation without appropriate filtering.

Don't let the SEO pool near M2 unfiltered. SEO signals can identify content and authority properties that have little direct local call-generation value.

Don't confuse exclusion with ranking. A candidate that has a naming-quality weakness may deserve a scoring penalty rather than automatic rejection.

Don't treat broad geographic relevance as equivalent to local specificity. City-level and state-level geographic signals have different commercial value.

Don't assume every geographic match is reliable. Short city names and common substrings can create false positives. Geographic matching needs appropriate disambiguation.

Evaluation Objectives
The pipeline is designed to:
- Process large volumes of expired-domain inventory.
- Reduce the candidate pool through staged evaluation.
- Reserve expensive checks for promising candidates.
- Produce a small, prioritized set for human acquisition decisions.
- Keep commercial scoring separate from technical health evaluation.
